Verdict: PASS. I wrote it to session_plan/eval_task_2.md.

I judged the diff and re-ran only cargo test --test module_size (28 passed). I didn't run the binary.

What the change does:
• Grok 4.6 rate: it goes back to xAI's base rate, $2 / $0.50 / $6, and $4 / $1 / $12 above 200K tokens.
• US endpoint premium: Grok 4.6 and Grok 4.7 cost 1.1x when base_url's host is us.api.x.ai. This applies to the session price, including Grok 4.7's yoagent preset price, and to the per-turn long-context pricing.
• User overrides: a [model_pricing] entry is used as written. Its early return runs before any scaling.
• Endpoint check: it compares the URL's host exactly. The table tests cover the path, query-string and lookalike-host cases.
• Old assertions: the Grok 4.6 values pinned by fc12df10 were changed to the new exact values, not loosened to contains().
• Every new definition has its caller in this diff, and cost.rs only gained the module line and the call sites.
• Docs: cost-tracking.md takes Grok 4.7 off the "reads low" list and says the endpoint now decides the rate.

Where it differs from the task, all minor:
• The check looks only at the host, not "provider is xai and host matches." The new module says why: a request to us.api.x.ai is billed at xAI's US rate whichever provider sent it.
• The setter is called in main.rs after the setup wizard rather than in cli.rs, because the wizard can set base_url on a first run. A test checks that order in the source.
• Model ids with a prefix, like xai/grok-4.6, don't get the premium. The docs say only the exact ids are priced this way.
